WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:16.949
on Hey, Flag!, we have three special guests from Europe.

2
00:00:21.652 --> 00:00:23.833
Flag! Tell us about yourself!

3
00:00:23.853 --> 00:00:28.356
"I am the flag of Denmark.

4
00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:32.885
Called the Dannebrog, I am over eight-hundred years old.

5
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:36.646
"Legend says I fell from heaven.

6
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:44.008
In the thirteenth century, King Valdemar II was fighting a battle—and losing.

7
00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:50.110
Suddenly a red banner with a white cross fell from the sky.

8
00:00:51.091 --> 00:00:55.612
The king and the Danish army thought my sudden appearance was a sign from God.

9
00:00:58.076 --> 00:01:03.217
Everyone was filled with courage to fight even harder, and the Danes won the battle.

10
00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:09.219
"Ever since then, I have been an important symbol to the Danish people.

11
00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:17.041
People proudly fly me on June 15, Valdemar's Day, to celebrate my miraculous appearance.

12
00:01:18.462 --> 00:01:20.582
But that's not the only day Danes celebrate me.

13
00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:27.404
People often decorate birthday cakes and Christmas trees with my image too.

14
00:01:29.484 --> 00:01:32.665
"Before I go, I have something else to brag about.

15
00:01:34.005 --> 00:01:37.546
My design inspired the flags of other Nordic countries.

16
00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:44.268
Finland, Sweden, Norway, and Iceland all have cross designs too."

17
00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:48.370
Hey, Flag!

18
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.870
Tell us about yourself!

19
00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:55.732
"I am the Union Jack, the flag of the United Kingdom.

20
00:01:57.452 --> 00:02:00.675
My design comes from the different countries that make up the UK.

21
00:02:02.016 --> 00:02:04.618
I am one of the most recognizable flags in the world.

22
00:02:04.638 --> 00:02:11.424
"A long time ago, England and Scotland were separate kingdoms with different flags.

23
00:02:12.926 --> 00:02:13.987
In England, St.

24
00:02:14.007 --> 00:02:15.708
George's Cross was on the flag.

25
00:02:16.949 --> 00:02:20.172
This is a red cross on a white background called a field.

26
00:02:21.573 --> 00:02:22.634
In Scotland, St.

27
00:02:22.755 --> 00:02:24.216
Andrew's Cross was on the flag.

28
00:02:25.224 --> 00:02:30.587
This is a diagonal white cross on a blue field.

29
00:02:30.687 --> 00:02:35.550
"In 1603 King James of Scotland became the king of England, uniting the two kingdoms.

30
00:02:36.871 --> 00:02:39.212
He wanted a new flag to represent this union.

31
00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:41.673
That's when I was created!

32
00:02:41.693 --> 00:02:49.638
"Almost two centuries later, I was redesigned because Ireland became part of the United Kingdom.

33
00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:53.340
St. Patrick is an important saint to Ireland.

34
00:02:54.884 --> 00:02:55.484
So St.

35
00:02:55.545 --> 00:02:57.466
Patrick's Cross was added to my design.

36
00:02:58.586 --> 00:03:01.308
This is a diagonal red cross on a white field.

37
00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:09.172
Though only Northern Ireland is in the UK today, my design has stayed the same.

38
00:03:09.192 --> 00:03:13.194
"You may have seen me on the flags of Australia and New Zealand.

39
00:03:14.395 --> 00:03:17.797
In fact, I appear on the flags of several other countries and places.

40
00:03:20.419 --> 00:03:21.239
Hey, Flag!

41
00:03:21.539 --> 00:03:22.760
Tell us about yourself!

42
00:03:25.352 --> 00:03:28.394
"My name is the Tricolore, which means three colors.

43
00:03:29.995 --> 00:03:31.195
I am the flag of France.

44
00:03:32.756 --> 00:03:36.518
I was created around 1789 during the French Revolution.

45
00:03:37.859 --> 00:03:42.381
That's when the French people removed their monarchy and set up the First French Republic.

46
00:03:44.102 --> 00:03:50.246
My design was seen to represent the ideals of the revolution: liberty, equality, and fraternity.

47
00:03:50.266 --> 00:03:54.528
"Why do I have red, white, and blue stripes?

48
00:03:55.848 --> 00:03:56.949
No one knows for sure!

49
00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:02.134
But people who supported the revolution wore red, white, and blue ribbons.

50
00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:06.978
And the colors do have other historical meanings.

51
00:04:08.079 --> 00:04:11.262
Red and blue are the colors of Paris, the capital of France.

52
00:04:13.024 --> 00:04:14.545
Red is associated with St.

53
00:04:14.565 --> 00:04:16.427
Denis, the protector of Paris.

54
00:04:17.748 --> 00:04:19.029
And blue is linked to St.

55
00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.432
Martin, who was known for helping the poor.

56
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:26.817
"Some people think my white stripe represents the nation.

57
00:04:28.178 --> 00:04:31.739
Others think it recognizes the old monarchy's white royal flag.

58
00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:38.762
"After I was officially adopted in 1794, France's politics remained stormy.

59
00:04:41.103 --> 00:04:43.604
Two decades later, France had a king again.

60
00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.046
I was replaced for a while by the white royal flag.

61
00:04:51.827 --> 00:04:52.708
I returned in 1830.

62
00:04:54.632 --> 00:04:58.699
Apart from a few days, I've proudly been the flag of France ever since."

63
00:05:01.763 --> 00:05:03.926
I hope you learned a lot from our guests.

64
00:05:05.228 --> 00:05:07.231
Your flag has a rich history.

65
00:05:08.353 --> 00:05:09.715
What does your flag mean?
